    "note": "APPROVE with zero MAJOR. The reviewer independently reproduced the exact 6/4/0 partition with two separate parsers, confirmed fixture 6's only non-ASCII byte is in its frontmatter description (the body is pure ASCII) and the narrow-40 set from line lengths. It ported every validator to a simulator plus an independent inverse checker and ran 167 deterministic probes, ~800,000 fuzzed and mutation inputs and a 300,000+ visual-gate fuzz with no fail-open, no hang and no verbatim/order invariant break, and explicitly re-attacked the frontmatter 'config : 42' spacing seam (this renderer trims the key from the first draft). One MINOR was applied: size and the annotation grid index used the signed-integer pair helper and so accepted a negative value, which is outside the grammar (a leading minus is legal only for label offsets); they now use an unsigned pair and two regression pins lock it. The NITs (quoted YAML visual keys, frontmatter-CRLF safe-direction fallback, the duplicated fence predicate) are shared safe-direction behavior with no corpus sample and are unchanged. The untrimmed frontmatter-key pattern in twelve earlier renderers remains a separate cross-family follow-up."
